forceTaskPrompt.en-US:
[Forced squash | attempt {attempt}] Context reached {tokens}, exceeding the forced threshold {threshold}. Stop the original task immediately. Until squash succeeds, do not continue implementation, explain, or call any other tools.

You may only:
1. Call session_log and choose a completed starting point that frees enough context;
2. Generate a task-state snapshot from the full current context;
3. Call session_squash once with both from and the complete summary.

Use these sections: ## Goal & Constraints; ## Work Completed (focus on what was done, its target, final outcome, and verification; do not repeat it); ## Current State (the exact In Progress stopping point, Remaining, and Blocked / Unknown); ## Decisions & Evidence; ## Artifacts (file, branch, commit, and log state); and ## Resume (first action and completion criteria). Completed work must not reappear under Remaining or Resume. Use VERIFIED, INFERRED, UNKNOWN, NOT VERIFIED, or BLOCKED when needed. Record only effective state needed to continue, absorbing task facts from earlier summaries while omitting squash, context-threshold, session_log, session_squash, and session-switching mechanics. Squash now even if the task is unfinished. Do not merely reply with text; complete the session_squash call.
